  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Figure 8.4(a), the weighted supermatrix W for the ANP example — a screenshot titled \"Super Decisions Main Window: Chapter_8_ANP.sdmod\". Clusters are L1-GOAL (Goal_Node), L2-Criteria (C1-C3) and L3-Alternatives (A1, A2). Unlike the AHP matrix in Figure 8.2(b), the criteria-to-criteria block is not zero (C1 column: C2 0.083333, C3 0.166667; C2 column: C1 0.125000, C3 0.125000; C3 column: C1 0.187500, C2 0.062500) and the alternatives feed back into the criteria (A1 column: C2 0.333333, C3 0.666667; A2 column: C2 0.500000, C3 0.500000). That non-zero feedback is the structural difference the chapter is illustrating.",
      "state": "draft",
      "drafted_by": {
        "kind": "agent",
        "id": "claude",
        "model": "claude-opus-5"
      },
      "drafted_at": "2026-09-29",
      "lang": "en"
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 8.4(a), la supermatrice pondérée W de l'exemple ANP — une capture d'écran intitulée « Super Decisions Main Window: Chapter_8_ANP.sdmod ». Les clusters sont L1-GOAL (Goal_Node), L2-Criteria (C1-C3) et L3-Alternatives (A1, A2). Contrairement à la matrice AHP de la figure 8.2(b), le bloc critères-critères n'est pas nul (colonne C1 : C2 0.083333, C3 0.166667 ; colonne C2 : C1 0.125000, C3 0.125000 ; colonne C3 : C1 0.187500, C2 0.062500) et les alternatives rétroagissent sur les critères (colonne A1 : C2 0.333333, C3 0.666667 ; colonne A2 : C2 0.500000, C3 0.500000). Cette rétroaction non nulle est la différence structurelle qu'illustre le chapitre.",
